{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14269 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that benzocaine is associated with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple indirect pathways. Benzocaine is identified as a target of NCI-H727, a compound that itself targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Similarly, benzocaine is also linked to Notoamide R and Talathermophilins A, which also target the same complex. These findings indicate that benzocaine may exert its biological effects through a series of molecular intermediates that ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores across all three paths are consistent, suggesting a potential role for benzocaine in modulating the activity of this epigenetic complex. The mechanism likely involves benzocaine acting as a ligand or inhibitor that influences the function of the complex, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
